# dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# build outputs
.next/
out/
dist/

# Expo (apps/mobile). `.expo/` is the local dev-server cache and generated
# types; `expo export` writes the bundle into `dist/`, which the unanchored
# entry above already matches at any depth.
#
# `android/` and `ios/` are ignored too — but from `apps/mobile/.gitignore`,
# not from here, and that placement is load-bearing rather than tidy. Read the
# header of that file before moving the rules up: @expo/fingerprint looks for
# them from the Expo project root when it has no git to ask, which is the case
# on an EAS worker, and a rule at this level is invisible to it. The 2026-08-26
# build failure that taught us so is in docs/mobile/eas-build-profiles.md.
.expo/

