# Playwright MCP session artifacts (screenshots, snapshots), and the page
# snapshots Microsoft's playwright-cli writes to CWD under its own directory
.playwright-mcp/
.playwright-cli/

# Graphify knowledge-graph output (local index, rebuilt on demand)
graphify-out/

# Scratch scripts from parallel QA agents (cursor / cowork / one-off seeding).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: on 2026-08-01 an untracked one-off dropped into scripts/ put
# `pnpm verify` in the red for work that had nothing to do with it, and every
# gate run after that had to be discounted by hand — which is exactly the kind
# of thing that later gets discounted when it IS real. biome.json sets
# `vcs.useIgnoreFile: true`, so an entry here takes the file out of the gate AND
# out of reach of a broad `git add` in one move.
#
# Convention: one-off scripts go in scripts/scratch/. Anything meant to survive
# gets a real name, a test, and a commit.
scripts/scratch/
scripts/bulk-cursor-pets-staging.mjs

# Playwright MCP writes snapshots and screenshots to CWD, which is the repo root.
# `.playwright-mcp/` above only covers the cases where it uses its own directory.
# Telling a browser agent "don't touch the repo" cannot prevent this — it is the
# tool's default, not the agent's choice. These are session artifacts: the .md is
# an accessibility-tree dump, the .png a screenshot. Neither is a finding.
/*.png
/*-snapshot.md
/panorama.md

# vitest --reporter=json output consumed by scripts/check-suite-coverage.ts
.vitest-report.json

# Local Definition-of-Done gate evidence (one dir per run: logs, .exit markers,
# the vitest JSON report). Reproduced by re-running the gate, never committed.
# ANCHORED AT THE ROOT on purpose: an unanchored `gate-*/` matches at ANY depth,
# so a future `docs/gate-chain/` or `scripts/gate-runner/` would stop being
# tracked in silence. The gate writes one directory per run at the repo root.
# .easignore carries this line verbatim (release-config.test.ts compares them
# rule for rule) — change both or that fence goes red.
/gate-*/

# QA session-minting output — carries live session tokens for seed accounts.
# The repo is public: this file must never be committable, same reasoning as
# e2e/.auth/ above.
qa-sessions*.json

# playwright-cli (the vendored .claude/skills/playwright-cli agent skill)
# writes browser storage state — cookies, localStorage, live session tokens —
# to CWD on request. Same reasoning as qa-sessions*.json above: the repo is
# public and none of these may ever be committable. Covers the auto-generated
# default name, the skill's own recommended save-file suffix
# (references/storage-state.md: "Add *.auth-state.json to .gitignore"), and
# the two names its own worked examples save to.
*.auth-state.json
*-auth-state.json
storage-state*.json
auth.json
my-session.json

# Firebase Admin SDK service-account keys — the FCM V1 credential that lets Expo
# deliver push on this project's behalf. Downloaded from Firebase → Project
# settings → Service accounts, uploaded once with `eas credentials`, and never
# stored here: the repo is public and this file is a PRIVATE KEY, not an
# identifier. Firebase names its download <project>-firebase-adminsdk-<id>.json,
# which the first pattern catches; the second covers a copy somebody renamed.
# .easignore carries both lines verbatim (release-config.test.ts compares them
# rule for rule) — change both or that fence goes red.
#
# NOT to be confused with `apps/mobile/google-services.json`, which is committed
# ON PURPOSE and must stay that way — that one carries public-facing identifiers
# and `expo config` fails without it. Two files, one console, opposite rules.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
service-account*.json

# A ROOT app.json is Expo debris. The real one is apps/mobile/app.json.
#
# `@expo/config`'s `modifyConfigAsync()` writes `path.join(projectRoot, "app.json")`
# whenever a config-mutating command runs and finds no static config at that root
# (Config.js: `config.staticConfigPath ?? path.join(projectRoot, 'app.json')`).
# Run any such command — `expo install`, `expo prebuild`, `eas update:configure`
# — from C:\dev\dim instead of from apps/mobile and Expo resolves the REPO ROOT
# as the project root, then leaves `{"expo": {}}` behind. Measured 2026-08-26:
# from the repo root `expo config` reads the root package.json and reports the
# WEB app's identity (name "dim", version 0.1.0), which is how it decides the
# root is a project at all.
#
# WHY NOT FIX THE CAUSE, since a symptom in .gitignore is normally the worse
# trade. There is no cause in this repo to fix, and that was measured rather than
# assumed. `pnpm verify` → `verify:mobile` runs three things and NONE of them
# emits the file: `pnpm --filter mimar typecheck`, `pnpm --filter mimar test`,
# and `pnpm --filter mimar exec expo config --type public` were each run with the
# root app.json deleted first, and it did not come back. `pnpm --filter mimar
# exec` reports `cwd = C:\dev\dim\apps\mobile`, which is correct — the repo's own
# invocation was never the one at fault. The file arrives from an ad-hoc `expo`
# or `eas` command typed at the repo root, and no package.json script can stop a
# human's cwd.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS ENOUGH TO IGNORE RATHER THAN DELETE. It is untracked, so a
# `git add -A` sweeps it into somebody's commit; the repo already bans `-A` for
# other reasons and this is one more. A committed root `app.json` would also be a
# static Expo config at the root of a monorepo whose real one is two directories
# down — harmless today (its `{"expo": {}}` merges to nothing over package.json,
# verified) and exactly the kind of shadow that stops being harmless the first
# time a tool globs `app.json` from the root.
/app.json

# Generated by scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.ts on prebuild/predev.
# Copies of files that live in node_modules; committing them would create a
# second source of truth that drifts silently on the next bump.
/public/maplibre/
